# What a release build carries; never committed. Without the config that names them no build
# needs these folders, so the gates pass on a clean checkout.
#
# The six programs (INS-002, S12 packaging 2.1): the builder's bundle step
# (src/builder/carried/) builds `anima`, `anima-local-hub`, `anima-hub`, `anima-database` and
# `anima-gateway` with cargo and `anima-link` with `link/build.sh`, from the job's commit, puts
# `binaries/<program>-<target-triple>` here (and, on macOS, `<program>-universal-apple-darwin`
# made with lipo), and passes them in `bundle.externalBin` in `--config` to `tauri build` and
# `tauri bundle`.
#
# The agent sidecar (MET-019, D-10 d). The release build must:
#   1. build `anima-daemon` for the app's target triple from the same commit;
#   2. place it at `binaries/anima-daemon-<target-triple>` (this folder);
#   3. pass `--config tauri.release.conf.json` to `tauri build`, which names it in `bundle.externalBin`.
/binaries/
#
# The PostgreSQL tree (S3 T11, S12 packaging 2.2): the bundle step runs
# `database-tree/build.sh`, which writes the tree here; `bundle.resources` carries it as
# `database`.
/database/
